{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"75907b97-16ca-420f-9931-422bb65dbb49","hook_name":"SessionStart:startup","hook_event":"SessionStart","output":"<!-- CLAUDE.md (filtered for: critical-context, execution-rules, what-map, summary, file-naming, memory-context-tools, memory-search, platform, environment) -->\n\n<platform>\n## Platform: Windows\r\n\r\nThis is a Windows environment. Always use PowerShell-compatible syntax for shell commands. Avoid Unix-specific line continuations (`\\`), path separators (`/` in shell commands), and bash-specific features (extglob, etc.). When writing scripts, prefer `.ps1` or `.cmd` files over `.sh` files. Test commands mentally for Windows compatibility before executing.\n</platform>\n\n<critical-context>\n## CRITICAL �?\" Must Follow Always\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Use `uv` for all Python operations. Never use `pip` directly or base environment.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Read a file before editing it. Never edit without reading first.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Archive instead of delete. Never permanently delete without explicit user approval.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Search claude-mem FIRST before answering personal/business questions. Fall back to MemPalace/QMD if no results.\n</critical-context>\n\n<execution-rules>\n## Execution Rules\r\n\r\n- When a plan has been created and approved, EXECUTE it immediately. Do not ask which step to start with.\r\n- When the user asks to install or set up something, actually complete the installation �?\" do not claim completion without verification.\r\n- Prefer the user's explicitly requested approach first. Only pivot to alternatives after the requested approach demonstrably fails.\n</execution-rules>\n\n<what-map>\n## WHAT �?\" Map\r\n\r\n- **Workspace:** `C:\\Users\\Jyue` �?\" home workspace (thinking layer)\r\n- **Identity:** `.claude/agents/identity/`\r\n- **Skills:** `.claude/skills/` (canonical); junction at `.cursor/skills/`\r\n- **Execution:** Notion �?\" tasks/tracking live there\r\n- **Platform:** Windows 11, PowerShell, n8n, claude-flow. Relative paths preferred.\n</what-map>\n\n<environment>\n## Environment Rules\r\n\r\n| Tool | Rule |\r\n|------|------|\r\n| Python | `uv` only (see CRITICAL) |\r\n| JS/TS | `nvm`/`npm`/`npx` |\r\n| System packages | `choco` or `winget` (not apt/yum) |\r\n| Docker | Already installed |\r\n| Cloud CLIs | `gcloud` for Google Cloud |\r\n\r\n**Installed:** uv (v0.8.6), nvm + node (v24.7.0), docker, choco, winget, gcloud (v554.0.0)\n</environment>\n\n<memory-search>\n## Memory Search (5 Backends)\r\n\r\n- **3 backends:** claude-mem (auto-capture), MemPalace (local ChromaDB semantic store), QMD (Notion/Serena code context), MEMORY.md (project notes)\r\n- **Default:** Search memory FIRST before answering personal/business questions. Skip for pure coding, current file contents, or public info.\r\n- **claude-mem is PRIMARY**, MemPalace is SECONDARY (local ~/.mempalace/palace). Both auto-sync via MCP tools.\n</memory-search>\n\n<summary>\n## Summary\r\n\r\nWHAT (map), WHY (thinking/execution), HOW (AGENTS.md first), CRITICAL rules. See AGENTS.md for scan order and progressive disclosure.\n</summary>\n\r\n","stdout":"<!-- CLAUDE.md (filtered for: critical-context, execution-rules, what-map, summary, file-naming, memory-context-tools, memory-search, platform, environment) -->\n\n<platform>\n## Platform: Windows\r\n\r\nThis is a Windows environment. Always use PowerShell-compatible syntax for shell commands. Avoid Unix-specific line continuations (`\\`), path separators (`/` in shell commands), and bash-specific features (extglob, etc.). When writing scripts, prefer `.ps1` or `.cmd` files over `.sh` files. Test commands mentally for Windows compatibility before executing.\n</platform>\n\n<critical-context>\n## CRITICAL �?\" Must Follow Always\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Use `uv` for all Python operations. Never use `pip` directly or base environment.\r\n- **CRITICAL:** Read a file before editing it. Never edit without reading first.\r\n- **C